        StringKey.BeekeeperLogSeedSprouted to "Your seed has sprouted.",
        StringKey.BeekeeperLogPlantWildflowers to "Wildflowers! Forager bees drift in.",
        StringKey.BeekeeperLogPlantBramble to "A bramble! Guard bees settle in its thorns.",
        StringKey.BeekeeperLogFirstPollen to "A forager comes home dusted in pollen.",
        StringKey.BeekeeperLogBeeBread to "You pack pollen and honey into bee bread.",
        StringKey.BeekeeperLogWoodenHive to "You move the bees into a wooden hive. They seem pleased.",
        StringKey.BeekeeperLogWaspRaidGuardsFmt to "The wasp helps itself to %@ honey. The guards keep every bee safe.",
        StringKey.BeekeeperLogShoeMissGuardsFmt to "Missed. The wasp helps itself to %@ honey. The guards keep every bee safe.",
        StringKey.HelpBeekeeperGardenTitle to "🌱 The Garden",
        StringKey.HelpBeekeeperGarden to "The Hippies and the wasps sometimes give you a seed, and you can see what kind it is. Plant it in your bed (it grows one seed at a time) and wait: each plant takes its own time to sprout, even while the app is closed, and gives your hive a specialty.\n\nWildflowers and clover give foraging: a steady 3 pollen a minute each. Pollen and honey make bee bread at The Workbench, and bee bread plus wax pays for moving your bees into a wooden hive, where the combs make more honey. A bramble gives guarding: the combs make 25% more honey. The willow (about an hour) gives nursing: the queen lays 50% faster, and eats bee bread faster too. The poplar (about 6 hours, a seed from the wasps once you trade with them) gives resin: the bees gather propolis, which goes into candles and the Propolis Seal. Clover takes about 12 hours.\n\nPaper from the wasps buys the Beekeeper's Notebook, with a note about each thing your hive can do.",
